{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",

  // TEST-ONLY. Never deployed: no account_id, no routes, no workers.dev
  // subdomain, and no deploy script references it. `workers_dev: false` is the
  // mechanism rather than the convention -- the absence of routes alone would
  // not stop a stray
  // `wrangler deploy --config workers/mock-ai/wrangler.jsonc`.
  //
  // It exists for a sharp reason, sharper than the one workers/mock-browser had
  // before #186 retired it: that mock stood in front of a binding which DID
  // have a local emulator, only an expensive one to start. Workers AI has NO
  // local emulator at all, and wrangler treats an `ai` binding whose
  // `remote` is undefined as remote. So the moment the root wrangler.jsonc
  // gained its `ai` binding, every harness that boots the site tried to open a
  // REAL remote proxy session against the account, and 8 of 14 suites failed
  // with "More than one account available but unable to select one in
  // non-interactive mode" -- this login can see both Ryan Lindsey and
  // Pixelsonly Racing, and a test-only Worker deliberately carries no
  // account_id to disambiguate with.
  //
  // Pinning an account would have been the wrong repair. It fixes the error
  // message and keeps the hazard: `npm test` would then need network and live
  // credentials on a required CI path, and could bill neurons. `bindingOverrides`
  // instead replaces the binding with a plain service binding pointed here,
  // which is local, so no remote session is started at all.
  //
  // This paragraph USED TO SAY that setting `"remote": false` on the root `ai`
  // binding "would also have silenced it, in one line and with no new files",
  // and rejected it only because it would disarm real AI under `wrangler dev`
  // for everyone, which is precisely what the embedding job built on this
  // binding needs. The second half still holds and is still the reason the cost
  // belongs in the test harness rather than in the config local development
  // reads. THE FIRST HALF WAS FALSE, and #144 is what measured it.
  //
  // `remote: false` silences nothing here. Measured 2026-09-17 on the sibling
  // `ai_search` binding, which wrangler classifies identically: with the flag
  // set and the override removed, the harness opened the remote proxy session
  // anyway. wrangler does have a validator that rejects `remote: false` for
  // this class of binding, which is what makes the old sentence sound
  // plausible, but it sits on the `wrangler dev` path and the harness never
  // calls it. So the one-line alternative was never an alternative: it would
  // have cost the local `ai` binding for nothing, and the suites would still
  // have failed.
  //
  // SINCE #144 THIS WORKER STANDS IN FRONT OF TWO BINDINGS, not one. Declaring
  // `ai_search` on the MCP Worker reproduced the failure above exactly: `npm
  // test` went from 80 files green to 32 failed. A second mock Worker would
  // have been byte-identical to this one, and the argument in tests/workers.ts
  // that retired workers/mock-browser -- a moving part protecting nothing --
  // applies to writing one, so both bindings resolve here.
  //
  // The name is what `bindingOverrides: { AI: "mock-ai", AI_SEARCH: "mock-ai" }`
  // resolves.
  "name": "mock-ai",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-02",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "workers_dev": false,
}
